CALLY AT SMALL m, found a small discrepancy, and inferred the defect was a constant factor. The real obstruction is ASYMPTOTIC (sqrt(m) growth) and no small-m numerical check can see it. A numerical spot-check can refute a claim but cannot characterise the failure mode. DECISION - WONTFIX, on Joe's direction: the runners demonstrably DO notice false statements and it is impossible to prove one, so a defective statement is self-limiting rather than dangerous; and this is a twenty-year-old prelim problem of which there are hundreds more, so repairing it a third time is not worth the tokens. The correct statement needs at least a sqrt(m) loss, but whether C*sqrt(m)*2^-m is PROVABLE is unknown, and the runner deliberately avoided asserting an unproved corrected rate. Marking the row wontfix keeps the honest sorry and the documented counterexample in the file rather than inventing a third statement nobody has checked. NOTE the BPM rows are excluded from this policy: they are published and peer-reviewed, so a defect there is a finding rather than corpus noise. BEHAVIOURAL: arm (a) components carried the proof AND exposed the false repair; arm (b) Zulip opened two Gram-Schmidt threads which gave implementation history but no quantitative stability estimate; arm (c) arXiv NOT attempted, correctly - fourth consecutive run where the route was known. RECALL: 0 surfaced. Cause identified this wake and it is self-inflicted: the loop's own RECEIPTS crowd memories out of the seed search, because receipts quote routes and standard results verbatim in :detail and there are hundreds of them. Measured at limit=40: 'zero' returns 40 receipts and 0 memories; 'inner' returns 39 and 1. Fixed by over-fetching 5x and filtering to :evidence/type :memory. This is the FIFTH distinct cause of recall-empty in this lane and the fourth that was plumbing."}, :recall-system :v1-enriched-ladder, :memory-use #:memory-use{:status :outcome-recorded, :surfaced-ids [], :domain :mathematics, :used-ids [], 