or work to vanish here — nothing else in the loop would have surfaced it.\n\n**State: 45 resolved, 17 untouched, 16 blocked-and-diagnosed, 4 in flight or pending.** Usage 17%.a94J04 surfaced something operationally important: **`YoungL2.lean` contains an axiom-clean `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel`, but it sits outside all configured Lake libraries and cannot be imported.** Proved work that's unreachable by build configuration. And it's the *third* file tonight with a stale pessimistic note. Verifying both:Confirmed: **`./YoungL2.lean` at the repo root, `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel` at line 200, zero sorries — fully proved and unreachable.** And the lakefile comment mentions a `lean_lib` added on 2026-07-30. Looking properly:**This has explicit precedent in the lakefile itself.** The comment documents that `ConstructionTargets` had exactly this defect until 2026-07-30 — \"the proved lemmas were therefore unreachable from the problems they were built for\" — and a `lean_lib` was added to fix it. **`YoungL2.lean` has the same problem and was missed.** Four declarations, zero sorries, unreachable. Fixing it with a backup and a build test:**The fix works.** `lake build YoungL2` succeeds and `import YoungL2` now resolves — the L² contraction is importable with exactly the signature a94J04 needs. Checking I haven't broken anything else:**a94J04's most valuable output isn't a proof — it's a build defect that made proved work unreachable, and I've fixed it.**\n\nThe runner reported that `YoungL2.lean` holds an axiom-clean `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel` but sits \"outside all configured Lake libraries.\" I verified: it's at the repo root, **4 declarations, zero sorries, no `[[lean_lib]]` entry** — so `import YoungL2` failed with \"unknown module prefix.\"\n\n**The lakefile itself documents this exact defect class.** A comment records that `ConstructionTargets` had no `lean_lib` until 2026-07-30, so *\"the proved lemm