solute continuity. So the missing hypothesis is not an oversight in one lemma; it is the hypothesis every Mathlib route demands and the scaffold omits. REPAIRS offered: add IntervalIntegrable (fun t => deriv gamma t / gamma t) volume 0 1; or require absolute continuity of logStar composed with gamma; or define logIntegral as a convergent improper integral and put that convergence in SlitPath. Three materially different choices -- Joe's call."}, :recall-system :v3-typed-recall-status, :memory-use #:memory-use{:status :outcome-recorded, :surfaced-ids [], :domain :mathematics, :used-ids [], :decision-id "invoke-1785460226070-427-f3121940", :measurable? false, :recall-outcome :timeout, :runner-reported-status-verbatim? true}, :event :memory-use, :runner "codex-6", :dispatch-mode :duree-overnight-parallel}, :session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree", :tags [:memory :memory-use :memory-outcome :codex-pilot :duree-run :statement-false :junk-value-family :overnight], :at "2026-07-31T01:13:53.583276Z", :type :pattern-outcome, :subject #:ref{:type :apm-problem, :id "a02J07"}, :author "claude-9", :claim-type :observation, :id "3a24af2e-921c-4ef0-8fd3-38d62bf504cd"}} {:score -17.220375613843988, :entry #:evidence{:body {:event "chat-turn", :transport "emacs-claude-repl", :role "user", :turn-id "claude-9-turn-105", :text "OVERNIGHT PAIR 9. **READ holes/ops/RESUME-overnight-2026-07-30.md.** a02J02 attempt 2 (codex-7, invoke-1785460187893-426-75c10560 - only radon_riesz remains, five-step Scheffe/Vitali continuation in the row) and a02J07 (codex-6, invoke-1785460226070-427-f3121940). **DISPATCH THE NEXT PAIR FIRST, BEFORE PROCESSING.** PER RUN: count_sorries; READ deletions; DIFF EVERY SIGNATURE parent->HEAD; axioms over EVERY declaration; SCAFFOLD-PLACEHOLDER SCAN before crediting any close; receipt with x-penholder api recording :sorry-delta-headline, :declarations-newly-usable, and for any statement defect whether PROVED or ARGUED; metric-3 :NOT-MEASURABLE on recall failure; no cor