ad stopped a fourth time, and the cause was new.** a94J04 and a94J07 both completed *while I was processing the scribe*. Their parks were consumed by completion, the long promote-and-amend block occupied the turn, and I ended with zero real parks.\n\n**Dispatch-first protects against ending a turn without dispatching. It does not protect against a turn long enough for the in-flight work to finish inside it.** The rule that follows: after any long processing block, re-check whether the chain still has a real park before finishing.\n\nI caught this myself rather than being rescued by the heartbeat — the first time. Dispatched two immediately and parked.\n\n**And two results are unprocessed.** a94J04 and a94J07 completed but were never verified or receipted; their bellbacks haven't arrived as turns. I've named both job ids in the new park payload with an instruction to collect them via the jobs endpoint first. A completed job whose result was never processed is the quietest way for work to vanish here — nothing else in the loop would have surfaced it.\n\n**State: 45 resolved, 17 untouched, 16 blocked-and-diagnosed, 4 in flight or pending.** Usage 17%.a94J04 surfaced something operationally important: **`YoungL2.lean` contains an axiom-clean `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel`, but it sits outside all configured Lake libraries and cannot be imported.** Proved work that's unreachable by build configuration. And it's the *third* file tonight with a stale pessimistic note. Verifying both:Confirmed: **`./YoungL2.lean` at the repo root, `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel` at line 200, zero sorries — fully proved and unreachable.** And the lakefile comment mentions a `lean_lib` added on 2026-07-30. Looking properly:**This has explicit precedent in the lakefile itself.** The comment documents that `ConstructionTargets` had exactly this defect until 2026-07-30 — \"the proved lemmas were therefore unreachable from the problems they were built for\" 