nly `:evidence/type :memory` — which would **strip the pattern-description rows it needs**. Checking:**Confirmed, and worse than I thought — my \"fix\" broke it two ways.** `proposal-search-rows` reads `(:results search-result)`, expecting the original **map**; my seam now returns a **vector**, so that's `nil` → zero rows. And it *already* does exactly the filtering I added (`:memory` **or** `pattern-description-row?`). My filter was redundant from the start and destructive in effect. Reverting:Still zero — so my seam filter wasn't the root cause, though the revert was still right (it was redundant and shape-breaking). Let me locate the actual break:The seam returns the right shape now — 30 results, first row is the **pattern-description for `riemann-darboux-api`**, exactly what the proposer wants, plus 2 memory rows. So the break is downstream, in the \"reviewed edge to a pattern endpoint **in DOMAIN**\" requirement:The final link is `recall-by-endpoints` on the pattern id. Probing it directly:Zero memories for both patterns — despite the patterns existing with `:domain :mathematics` and the memories attached via `:memory/assert` edges with the pattern as an endpoint. Before asserting a cause, let me run the control that distinguishes \"projection broken\" from \"our edges misconfigured\":**Decisive.** `tactic-algebra-interference` returns **5 memories**; every pattern the codex-lane promotion pipeline has written to returns **0**. The projection works — our *edges* are wrong. Comparing a working memory's attachment against one of mine:I have enough for a clear diagnosis, and I'm going to stop digging rather than guess at a fix. Committing and recording:**I found the root cause of the entire recall history, and it's upstream of all seven causes I diagnosed today.**\n\n`recall-by-endpoints` returns **0 memories for every pattern this lane's promotion pipeline has ever written to** — riemann-darboux, measure-integration, holomorphic-disk, inner-product-space, missing