k-value defect class (a01A10 proved false, a01J01 argued vacuous), and the nine amendments applied.** ON DEADLINE: GET both, report honestly.\n\n--- resumed: parked dependencies complete (2) ---\n• invoke-1785457030310-419-0dd760eb: Completed the first lemma and formally refuted the second as currently modeled.\n\nRoute and search:\n\n- Intended standard result: Jensen’s formula gives linear zero-count growth; dyadic shell summation then gives convergence for exponent \\(\\alpha>1\\).\n- The required invariant is absent: `ProblemData.zeros` is unrelated to `zeroCount`, which is identically zero.\n- Arm (a) carried the result through `Summable.tendsto_atTop_zero` and limit uniqueness.\n- Queries:\n  - Loogle: `Lean Summable constant sequence iff zero`\n  - LeanSearch: `Mathlib constant sequence not summable one`\n  - Loogle: `\"Summable\" \"fun _ => 1\"`\n  - Local: `summable_const|not.*summable.*one|summable.*constant|Summable.*fun.*1`\n  - Zulip: `Jensen.*formula|zero count|zero-count|summable.*zero`\n- Loogle/LeanSearch returned no direct constant-one result. Local search found `Summable.tendsto_atTop_zero` and `Set.Finite.of_summable_const`.\n- Zulip returned generic summability and PNT discussions, but no relevant formalized Jensen/zero-enumeration bridge.\n- Arm (b) therefore came back empty. Arm (c) was not needed because the target was formally refuted. Literature anchor: none found.\n\nChanges in `problems/a01J06/lean/Main.lean`:\n\n- Completed `zeroCountLinear_of_expBound` using the existing identically-zero `zeroCount`.\n- Added `unconstrainedZerosCounterexample`, with `zeros n = 0`.\n- Proved its zero-count hypothesis.\n- Proved every associated weight equals one.\n- Proved axiom-clean that this weight sequence is not summable.\n- Left `weight_summable_of_zeroCountLinear` unresolved because the counterexample refutes it.\n- Sorry count: 2 → 1.\n\nExact obstruction:\n\n```lean\nunconstrainedZerosCounterexample.zeroCountLinear\n```\n\nholds, while:\n\n```le