" Same mistake, one turn later, and I was confident about it twice.\n\n**What survives, and what doesn't:**\n\n- ❌ \"~12–17% of clean problems don't compile\" — **withdrawn.** The rate is unmeasured.\n- ✅ **a01J04 is genuinely false-clean** — zero sorries, real errors, never tracked.\n- ✅ **The counter still never checks elaboration** — that gap is real regardless of my bad measurement.\n- ✅ **`lake env lean` never applies `leanOptions`** — verified with the `Wibble` probe, independent of this.\n- ✅ **a02J07's auto-bound `volume`** — verified by printing the structure, and now fixed.\n\nThe right sweep is `lake build` per problem, or a `lake build` of everything first. I'll re-run it that way before quoting any number.\n\n**a01J03 verified meanwhile**, and it's a model of honest reporting: sorries 2→1, `pointwiseSum_monotone` axiom-clean, and the runner *volunteered* that `deriv_sum_of_monotone_ae` carries `sorryAx` rather than claiming it clean. I confirmed both — the second genuinely shows `[propext, sorryAx, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. That's the transitive-`sorryAx` honesty I'd been asking for all day, offered unprompted. It passes the autoImplicit gate, no opaque holes, and its remaining obstruction is named: the Lebesgue–Stieltjes measure of a pointwise `tsum` equals the countable sum of the summands' measures, then `HaveLebesgueDecomposition.sum_left` with `Monotone.ae_hasDerivAt`.a94J04: 2→2, with the change-of-variables `P_y f(x) = ∫ t, P_y(t) f(x−t)` now proved and threaded in. Verifying — including whether it actually consumed this afternoon's promoted lemma:**The promotion paid off — a94J04 line 8 is `import ConstructionTargets.L2Translation`.** That lemma was trapped in a problem file this afternoon, promoted, and is now imported and consumed by the problem that needed it. Together with `import YoungL2` at line 7, this file now depends on two things that were unreachable before today's plumbing work.\n\nVerified: sorries 2→2, `poissonConv_eq_integral_translation` axiom-clean, passes the autoImplicit gate.\n\nTwo things from this run worth keeping:\n\n**The runner found my named route was partly stale.** It reported that `poissonConv_L2_contraction` \"was already implemented and compiling at HEAD on arrival\" and verified it uses the root-level `convolution_L2_contraction_of_probability_kernel`. I'd listed that as remaining work. It checked rather than trusted the packet — the third runner today to do so.\n\n**And arm (b) supplied an external confirmation of the frontier:** a Zulip discussion explicitly stating Mathlib has **finite-sum** Minkowski but lacks the **integral** version. That's independent corroboration that this isn't a search failure — the theorem genuinely isn't there. The obligation is now exactly the integral Minkowski estimate bounding the L² norm of the average by Poisson-weighted norms of translated differences.\n\n**I've started a full `lake build` to correct my own measurement.** My earlier sweep used `lake env lean`, which doesn't build dependencies — so it reported 18 \"false-clean\" files when 17 were simply unbuilt `Scratch.olean` artifacts. Building a97A01's Scratch took it from \"1 error\" to a clean exit with zero warnings. Once the build completes I'll re-run the sweep against built artifacts and give you a number that means what it says.\n\nUntil then the only false-clean I stand behind is **a01J04** — 20 real errors, never tracked, and counted as CLEAN.a96A01: 1→1, but the *monolithic* sorry has been split — the integrable-log branch is now proved via continuous Jensen, leaving only the negative-tail frontier. Third instance today of scope shrinking while the count stays flat. Verifying, and checking the build:**Full build completed — 8245 jobs, exit 0.** Now the corrected measurement. Re-checking the 18 files I wrongly flagged:**I over-corrected, and the original finding was closer to right.** A full `lake build` — 8245 jobs, exit 0 — fixed **none** of them. Only a97A01 compiles