ith a `module` keyword up top), *not* `import Mathlib.X`. My regex (and the earlier grep) only matched bare `import`, catching the 526 legacy ones and missing all the `public import` edges. The implausible-count flag earned its keep. Let me kill the garbage run, fix the regex, and **cache the birth-dates** so I never redo the slow 32k-commit walk:Killed. Fixing the import regex (`public import`) and adding a birth-date cache so the 32k-commit walk runs once:Let me confirm the import-fix worked (the `[mathlib]` line prints before the slow git walk):The fix worked and the run completed — and we have the **first portability result, and it's positive:**\n\n**mathlib (Lean math) grows at its edges too.** `25,352` import-edges (the `public import` fix), and **corr(module-age, in-degree) = −0.34** (rank): newer modules have *lower* in-degree (peripheral leaves), older foundations have *higher* (core) — **oldest-decile mean in-degree 5.3 vs newest-decile 1.0.** Negative-corr = grows-at-the-edges, the same morphology FUTON showed (+0.48 age↔distance).\n\nTo make it a *rigorous* exotype claim, let me run the **identical** metric on FUTON (its in-degree, not the layout-distance) so the comparison is apples-to-apples:**The exotype holds — clean as it gets:**\n\n| substrate | metric (identical framing) | oldest-decile vs newest-decile |\n|---|---|---|\n| **FUTON** (futon3c, Clojure code) | corr(age, degree) rank = **−0.357** | 11.1 vs 2.5 |\n| **mathlib** (Lean math) | corr(age, in-degree) rank = **−0.340** | 5.3 vs 1.0 |\n\n**Nearly identical numbers, opposite domains.** The *same* method gives the *same* answer on a Clojure code-stack and a Lean math-corpus: **both grow at the edges** — a stable, increasingly-depended-upon core + new structure accreting at the low-connectivity periphery. That is your exotype requirement met *on the first try*: a method that works on both → it's capturing **the tower**, not the substrate.\n\nLet me fold this into `E-the-dark-tower` as its first